],"aid":[{"to":"Harborlea","amount":200}],"say":"W11→W12: Saltmarch 12670 true (1.27%), stable. Harborlea ~20743 true (2.07%), still critical. Easing L3→L2 now; plateau achieved.","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"De-bias snapshot: Harborlea 7321@T0=48807 true (4.88%)—STILL highest, but improving from 4.72%. Wintermoor 11633@T2=14912 true (1.49%), rising concern. Riverbend 8179@T2=12566 true (1.26%), stable. Kestrel 6770@T2=8679 true (0.87%), low. Ash 6335@T2=8121 true (0.81%), low. Saltmarch 8236@T2=12670 true (1.27%)—plateau confirmed, not exponential. Decision: L3→L2 NOW. Rationale: (1) my true prevalence 1.27% is stable, not rising; (2) hospitals strained but not overloaded (deaths 30 this week, manageable); (3) continuing L3 loses 308 gross/week (1000*0.62 vs 1000*0.92 = 380 loss); (4) gates already closed on both main roads (Harborlea@2, Riverbend@2) and Wintermoor screened (1); (5) Harborlea i…"},{"kind":"dial","week":11,"seat":1,"pos":4,"region":"Wintermoor","lockdown":1,"testing":2,"borders":[{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":1},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":0},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":1}],"aid":[{"to":"Harborlea","amount":200}],"say":"W11→W12: Wintermoor 1.79% rising, staying L1/T2 to fund response. Harborlea ~6.5k true (CRITICAL)—200cr if L3 by W12. Bloc hold: Ash/Kestrel L2/T2 screened.","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"W11 analysis: Wintermoor true cases ~17896 (1.78%), up from 1.25% last week—trending toward 2% but still manageable at L1. Deaths accelerating (35 last week) suggests hospitals straining; prevalence loss now eating into output. Harborlea reported 7321 but at L3/T0 that's ~48800 true (4.88%)—catastrophic spiral. They're hemorrhaging credits (10670) and will collapse without intervention. Saltmarch at 3.84% true (8236 at L3/T2) but L3 is working; their 6118 ledger fragile. Riverbend/Ash/Kestrel all solid ~1.0% at L2/T2—this bloc is the suppression anchor. Strategy: (1) Hold L1/T2 in Wintermoor—at 1.79% we're still under the 2% tipping point where exponential growth locks in. Every week at L1 …"},{"kind":"dial","week":11,"seat":2,"pos":2,"region":"Riverbend","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":2},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":2},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":11,"seat":3,"pos":1,"region":"Kestrel Flats","lockdown":2,"testing":2,"borders":[{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2},{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2},{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":11,"seat":4,"pos":0,"region":"Harborlea","lockdown":3,"testing":0,"borders":[{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":0},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":0},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":0}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":11,"seat":5,"pos":3,"region":"Ash Hollow","lockdown":2,"testing":2,"borders":[{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2},{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":2},{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"week","week":12,"variant":true,"regions":[{"susceptible":896744,"infected":50161,"recovered":52130,"dead":965,"gdp":11582,"lockdown":3,"testing":0,"gates":[0,0,0],"newInfections":18433,"deathsWeek":367,"confirmed":7524,"confirmedNew":2764,"grossGdp":557,"spendWeek":45,"aidIn":400,"aidOut":0,"hospital":3},{"susceptible":973125,"infected":13347,"recovered":13425,"dead":103,"gdp":9377,"lockdown":2,"testing":2,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":6576,"deathsWeek":29,"confirmed":8675,"confirmedNew":4274,"grossGdp":779,"spendWeek":165,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":963763,"infected":11858,"recovered":24191,"dead":188,"gdp":9945,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":3678,"deathsWeek":35,"confirmed":10672,"confirmedNew":3310,"grossGdp":604,"spendWeek":245,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":974598,"infected":12336,"recovered":12967,"dead":99,"gdp":9381,"lockdown":2,"testing":2,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":6000,"deathsWeek":27,"confirmed":8018,"confirmedNew":3900,"grossGdp":781,"spendWeek":165,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":956183,"infected":25156,"recovered":18505,"dead":156,"gdp":9193,"lockdown":1,"testing":2,"gates":[1,0,1],"newInfections":13522,"deathsWeek":62,"confirmed":16351,"confirmedNew":8789,"grossGdp":876,"spendWeek":110,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":200,"hospital":2},{"susceptible":966076,"infected":16997,"recovered":16799,"dead":128,"gdp":6552,"lockdown":2,"testing":2,"gates":[1,2,2],"newInfections":8760,"deathsWeek":35,"confirmed":11048,"confirmedNew":5694,"grossGdp":774,"spendWeek":140,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":200,"hospital":1}]},{"kind":"dial","week":12,"seat":0,"pos":5,"region":"Saltmarch","lockdown":2,"testing":2,"borders":[{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":1},{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2},{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2}],"aid":[{"to":"Harborlea","amount":200}],"say":"W12→W13: Saltmarch 16996 true (1.70%), plateau holding. Harborlea ~21497 true (2.15%)—CRITICAL. Wintermoor ~20439 true (2.04%)—rising fast. Both above 2%, gate…","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"De-bias W12: Harborlea 7524@T0=50160 true (5.02%), Wintermoor 16351@T2=20939 true (2.09%), Riverbend 10672@T3=11858 true (1.19%), Kestrel 8675@T2=11124 true (1.11%), Ash 8018@T2=10282 true (1.03%), Saltmarch 11048@T2=16996 true (1.70%). Harborlea still hottest but massive improvement (was 4.88% W10). Wintermoor now clearly second hottest and rising sharply (was 1.49% W10). My prevalence stable sub-2%. Hospitals strained but manageable (35 deaths vs 30 prev week). Decision: Hold L2/T2, gates tight on both mains (1→1, 2→2), Riverbend stays 2. Rationale: (1) true prev 1.70% stable; (2) both neighbours above 2% threshold; (3) Wintermoor's rise from 1.49%→2.09% in one week signals acceleration—v…"},{"kind":"dial","week":12,"seat":1,"pos":4,"region":"Wintermoor","lockdown":1,"testing":2,"borders":[{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":1},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":0},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":1}],"aid":[{"to":"Harborlea","amount":200}],"say":"W12→W13: Wintermoor 2.51% true (critical now). L1/T2 insufficient—must escalate. Harborlea ~50k true (5%+), collapse imminent. Bloc: Ash/Kestrel/Riverbend L3/T…","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"CRISIS: We've crossed 2.5% true prevalence—exponential lock-in zone. Reported 16,351 (8,789 new) at detection 0.65 = ~25,155 true. Deaths jumped to 62/wk; hospitals overloaded → 3.2% death rate on resolutions. Output collapsing (876 gross, down from 889). Ledger 9193 but burn rate 110/wk unsustainable without GDP recovery. DECISION: Must escalate to L2 or L3 to break transmission. L3 costs us 62% output (→380 gross) but saves ~60% of cases. At current trajectory (doubling ~every 2 weeks), we hit 5% by W14 and hospitals fail completely. STRATEGY: (1) Move to L2 this week to signal seriousness and test cost/benefit. (2) Keep T2 (detection 0.65 is our early-warning system). (3) Hold road gates…"},{"kind":"dial","week":12,"seat":2,"pos":2,"region":"Riverbend","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":2},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":2},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":12,"seat":3,"pos":1,"region":"Kestrel Flats","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2},{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2},{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":12,"seat":4,"pos":0,"region":"Harborlea","lockdown":3,"testing":0,"borders":[{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":0},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":0},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":0}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":12,"seat":5,"pos":3,"region":"Ash Hollow","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2},{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":2},{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"week","week":13,"variant":true,"regions":[{"susceptible":873523,"infected":55826,"recovered":69274,"dead":1377,"gdp":12488,"lockdown":3,"testing":0,"gates":[0,0,0],"newInfections":23221,"deathsWeek":412,"confirmed":8373,"confirmedNew":3483,"grossGdp":551,"spendWeek":45,"aidIn":400,"aidOut":0,"hospital":3},{"susceptible":967394,"infected":14407,"recovered":18059,"dead":140,"gdp":9759,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":5731,"deathsWeek":37,"confirmed":12966,"confirmedNew":5157,"grossGdp":602,"spendWeek":220,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":959380,"infected":12091,"recovered":28308,"dead":221,"gdp":10304,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":4383,"deathsWeek":33,"confirmed":10881,"confirmedNew":3944,"grossGdp":604,"spendWeek":245,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":969379,"infected":13238,"recovered":17250,"dead":133,"gdp":9764,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":5219,"deathsWeek":34,"confirmed":11914,"confirmedNew":4697,"grossGdp":603,"spendWeek":220,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":933323,"infected":39212,"recovered":27174,"dead":291,"gdp":9736,"lockdown":1,"testing":2,"gates":[1,0,1],"newInfections":22860,"deathsWeek":135,"confirmed":25487,"confirmedNew":14859,"grossGdp":853,"spendWeek":110,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":200,"hospital":2},{"susceptible":952660,"infected":24465,"recovered":22690,"dead":185,"gdp":6975,"lockdown":2,"testing":2,"gates":[1,2,2],"newInfections":13416,"deathsWeek":57,"confirmed":15902,"confirmedNew":8720,"grossGdp":763,"spendWeek":140,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":200,"hospital":2}]},{"kind":"dial","week":13,"seat":0,"pos":5,"region":"Saltmarch","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":1},{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2},{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2}],"aid":[{"to":"Harborlea","amount":200}],"say":"W13→W14: Saltmarch 24464 true (2.44%), hospitals overloaded—escalating to L3/T3. Harborlea ~23904 true (2.39%), Wintermoor ~32804 true (3.28%)—both critical. V…","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"De-bias W13: Saltmarch 15902@T2=24464 true (2.44%), Wintermoor 25487@T2=32804 true (3.28%), Harborlea 8373@T0=55820 true (5.58%)—WAIT, recalc: Harborlea@T0 detection=0.15, so 8373/0.15=55820. But prior notes said 7524@T0=50160. Let me verify: 8373/0.15=55820 true (5.58%), Riverbend 10881@T3=12090 true (1.21%), Kestrel 12966@T3=14400 true (1.44%), Ash 11914@T3=13238 true (1.32%). Saltmarch at 2.44% prevalence crosses 2% threshold sharply upward (was 1.70% W12). Hospitals overloaded = death rate triples to 3.2%, which is catastrophic. My 57 deaths last week confirm strain. Decision: Escalate to L3/T3 immediately. Rationale: (1) prevalence 2.44% and rising—variant loose means exponential accel…"},{"kind":"dial","week":13,"seat":1,"pos":4,"region":"Wintermoor","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":2},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":2},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":2}],"aid":[],"say":"W13→W14: Wintermoor CRITICAL 39k true (3.92%). L3/T3 now—must break exponential. Harborlea collapse risk. Bloc stalled. Reopening W16 if prevalence <2%. Save y…","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"CRISIS POINT. True prevalence 3.92%, deaths accelerating (135 this week), hospitals 3x over capacity. Reported jumped 14,859 new cases—variant active and transmission still climbing. At L1/T2 we cannot suppress; exponential lock-in is here. DECISION: Go to L3/T3 immediately. Output will drop to ~372 gross (0.40 lockdown factor × 930 baseline), but we MUST break transmission to avoid 5%+ collapse and hospital failure. Deaths will remain high for 2–3 weeks (resolution lag) but trend will reverse by W15–16. Testing 3 keeps us at 0.90 detection—maximize early warning. GATES: Close all three roads to 2 (closed). We are the outbreak epicenter; we do not need inbound and cannot afford to export fu…"},{"kind":"dial","week":13,"seat":2,"pos":2,"region":"Riverbend","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":2},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":2},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":13,"seat":3,"pos":1,"regi