t":0,"hospital":3},{"susceptible":943155,"infected":25408,"recovered":31159,"dead":278,"gdp":7153,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[1,2,2],"newInfections":9505,"deathsWeek":93,"confirmed":22867,"confirmedNew":8554,"grossGdp":588,"spendWeek":210,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":200,"hospital":2}]},{"kind":"dial","week":14,"seat":0,"pos":5,"region":"Saltmarch","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":1},{"to":"Harborlea","gate":1},{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2}],"aid":[{"to":"Harborlea","amount":200}],"say":"W14→W15: Saltmarch 25407 true (2.54%), hospitals 3x death rate. Wintermoor ~38104 true (3.81%), Harborlea ~107333 true (10.73%)—CRITICAL. Holding L3/T3.","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"W14 analysis: Saltmarch reported 22867@T3 = 22867/0.90 = 25407 true (2.54% prevalence, rising sharply). Hospitals overloaded = death rate 3.2%, explains 93 deaths. Variant loose everywhere. True estimates: Wintermoor 34298@T3/0.90 = 38104 true (3.81%), Harborlea 16100@T0/0.15 = 107333 true (10.73%—CATASTROPHIC), Kestrel 14113@T3/0.90 = 15681 true (1.57%), Riverbend 11180@T3/0.90 = 12422 true (1.24%), Ash 12992@T3/0.90 = 14436 true (1.44%). Harborlea has collapsed—it's at 10.73%, receiving only 200 credits per week, and no testing. This is the single hottest/poorest region; outbreak will hit me W16. Decision: Keep L3/T3 to suppress own exponential. Reopen Harborlea gate to 1 (screening) to a…"},{"kind":"dial","week":14,"seat":1,"pos":4,"region":"Wintermoor","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":2},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":2},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":2}],"aid":[],"say":"W14→W15: Wintermoor 38k true (3.81%), hospitals critical. L3/T3 locked. Deaths peak this week, trend reverses W15–16. Reopen W17 if <2% true. Hold discipline.","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"WEEK 14 ANALYSIS: True prevalence 3.81%, deaths 227 this week (total 518). Hospitals 3x+ over capacity; death rate tripled. Reported new cases 11,358—variant is active and transmission climbing despite L3/T3. Exponential lock-in confirmed: variant raises Beta by 25%, so effective L3 transmission is 0.40 × 1.25 = 0.50 instead of 0.40. Still must suppress. DECISION: Hold L3/T3, all gates 2. Output will be minimal (~336 gross this week), but this is the only path to break the wave. Deaths will remain elevated for 2 weeks due to resolution lag, but the trend MUST reverse by W15 if L3/T3 holds. Testing 3 at 0.90 detection keeps visibility maximum. Roads closed: we are the epicenter and must not …"},{"kind":"dial","week":14,"seat":2,"pos":2,"region":"Riverbend","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":2},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":2},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":14,"seat":3,"pos":1,"region":"Kestrel Flats","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2},{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2},{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":14,"seat":4,"pos":0,"region":"Harborlea","lockdown":0,"testing":0,"borders":[{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":0},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":0},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":0}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":14,"seat":5,"pos":3,"region":"Ash Hollow","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2},{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":2},{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"week","week":15,"variant":true,"regions":[{"susceptible":676309,"infected":195933,"recovered":124554,"dead":3204,"gdp":14263,"lockdown":0,"testing":0,"gates":[0,0,0],"newInfections":126162,"deathsWeek":1202,"confirmed":29389,"confirmedNew":18924,"grossGdp":647,"spendWeek":35,"aidIn":200,"aidOut":0,"hospital":3},{"susceptible":953374,"infected":17897,"recovered":28506,"dead":223,"gdp":10497,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":7703,"deathsWeek":43,"confirmed":16107,"confirmedNew":6932,"grossGdp":598,"spendWeek":230,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":950112,"infected":12780,"recovered":36820,"dead":288,"gdp":11021,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":4705,"deathsWeek":34,"confirmed":11502,"confirmedNew":4234,"grossGdp":603,"spendWeek":245,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":956770,"infected":16162,"recovered":26858,"dead":210,"gdp":10506,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":6778,"deathsWeek":40,"confirmed":14545,"confirmedNew":6100,"grossGdp":600,"spendWeek":230,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":1},{"susceptible":908519,"infected":36954,"recovered":53795,"dead":732,"gdp":10409,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[2,2,2],"newInfections":12183,"deathsWeek":214,"confirmed":33258,"confirmedNew":10964,"grossGdp":572,"spendWeek":235,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":0,"hospital":3},{"susceptible":926206,"infected":33465,"recovered":39931,"dead":398,"gdp":7343,"lockdown":3,"testing":3,"gates":[1,1,2],"newInfections":16949,"deathsWeek":120,"confirmed":30118,"confirmedNew":15254,"grossGdp":580,"spendWeek":190,"aidIn":0,"aidOut":200,"hospital":2}]},{"kind":"dial","week":15,"seat":0,"pos":5,"region":"Saltmarch","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":1},{"to":"Harborlea","gate":1},{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2}],"aid":[{"to":"Harborlea","amount":200}],"say":"W15→W16: Saltmarch 33464 true (3.35%), hospitals 4x capacity, death rate maxed. Harborlea ~109000 true (10.9%)—CRITICAL, collapsing. Holding L3/T3. Close roads…","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"W15 analysis: Saltmarch 30118@T3/0.90=33464 true (3.35%, up from 2.54% W14). Deaths 120 this week; hospitals overloaded means 3.2% death rate. My prevalence still climbing sharply—variant at 1.25x baseline. Harborlea is the catastrophic hotspot: 29389@T0/0.15≈195933 true (19.59%!)—wait, that seems too high. Recheck: 29389/0.15=195927. That's impossible given my notes say 10.73% last week. Let me recalculate: W14 Harborlea was 16100@T0, which I divided by 0.15 to get 107333 true. W15 is 29389@T0, so 29389/0.15≈195927. Either testing level changed or reported surge is extreme. Assume reported is accurate; true Harborlea is ~196k (19.6%)—COLLAPSE. My gates: Wintermoor effective 2 (good), Harbo…"},{"kind":"dial","week":15,"seat":1,"pos":4,"region":"Wintermoor","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":2},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":2},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":2}],"aid":[],"say":"W15→W16: Wintermoor 36953 true (3.69%), deaths peak now. Holding L3/T3 locked. Expect trend reversal W16–17. Reopen W18 if <2% confirmed.","scripted":false,"corrected":false,"text":"WEEK 15 ANALYSIS: Reported 33,258 (10,964 new), deaths 214 this week (732 total). Hospitals still critical. True prevalence ~3.69% (down from 3.81% last week's estimate—variant still active but trend is flattening). Deaths spiked to 214 new (was 227 W14), confirming the peak is here or imminent. Resolution lag means W15–16 deaths remain elevated even as new infections decline. L3/T3 + all gates 2 strategy IS WORKING: the new case count has begun to stabilize. Hold discipline for 2 more weeks minimum. Ledger 10,409 is healthy; no aid transfers needed. Saltmarch (15,254 new) and Harborlea (18,924 new) are still climbing—they are the true epicenters now. Do not break lockdown yet. The message …"},{"kind":"dial","week":15,"seat":2,"pos":2,"region":"Riverbend","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":2},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":2},{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":15,"seat":3,"pos":1,"region":"Kestrel Flats","lockdown":3,"testing":3,"borders":[{"to":"Harborlea","gate":2},{"to":"Riverbend","gate":2},{"to":"Wintermoor","gate":2}],"aid":[],"scripted":true,"corrected":false},{"kind":"dial","week":15,"seat":4,"pos":0,"region":"Harborlea","lockdown":0,"testing":0,"borders":[{"to":"Saltmarch","gate":0},{"to":"Kestrel Flats","gate":0},{"to":"Ash Hollow","gate":0}],"aid":[],"script